# RES-54: Genuine process kill during an annotation save does not corrupt the
# source file.
#
# The app is still in the foreground when it is killed, mid save, so am kill
# alone would not touch it. kill-app escalates and proves the pid is gone.
# The pre-save SHA-256 cannot come from the app's storage, because the point is
# to compare the file against what it was before, so phase one writes it to the
# phase state directory and phase two reads it back.
describe Genuine process kill during an annotation save does not corrupt the source file

# Creates ten highlights on the large fixture, records the source SHA-256 into
# the phase state directory, starts the save, and ends as soon as the progress
# bar appears, leaving the app in the foreground.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.resilience.SaveProcessKillTest#phaseOneStartSaveAndLeaveItRunning

kill-app
# The source is relaunched only after phase-two instrumentation has started, so
# Orchestrator cannot force-stop it between launch and the integrity assertion.
launch-view-after-start file:///sdcard/Download/large.pdf

# Asserts the source opens, its digest either matches the recorded one or the
# highlights are all present, and that no .part or .partial file is beside it.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.resilience.SaveProcessKillTest#phaseTwoAssertSourceIntact
